  "reply_text": "Found one issue I’d fix before merging:\n\n**[P2] `topTags` mutates the input, breaking the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`  \n`tags.sort(...)` sorts the caller’s array in place. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud first and then reads `tags.slice(0, 5)`, the “recent” strip becomes the five highest-count tags rather than the first five tags in the original order. This also violates the README’s explicit non-mutation contract.\n\nReproduced with six tags: expected recent `first, second, third, fourth, fifth`; actual result `second, sixth, third, fifth, fourth`.\n\nSuggested fix: sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`) and add regression tests for input preservation and the sidebar’s recent order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but none checks this behavior. No files changed.",
